// The bitmap font (emo-desktop A8.1): the glyphs the fb core's labels
// render in, and the font's home per D3 — the glyph table is a literal
// in this module, the codegen's wide literals carrying it to the metal,
// so a frame's text needs no disk and no second image. The design is the
// project's own, drawn in `glyphs/glyphs.txt` and written into the `rows`
// table below by `glyphs/gen.py` (the gate refuses a stale table); the
// metrics are the fixed 8x16 cell the box model has measured labels by
// since A7.1, so the layout a frame had before its text is the layout
// its text lands in.
//
// The table is four 32-bit words per glyph, each word four rows with the
// topmost in the high byte, and a row's left pixel its high bit — the
// width the hosted emitters' Int64 literals all carry unsigned, packed
// four to a word so the 96 glyphs are 384 boxed cells on the metal's
// arena rather than 1,536. The 95 printable ASCII characters sit in code
// order, and the 96th glyph is what every other character shows as: the
// hollow cell. A `Surface` takes a glyph as two 64-bit words, the top
// eight rows and the bottom eight, which `top_rows` and `bottom_rows`
// assemble from the table's pairs.

def cell_w() Int64 {
  return 8
}

def cell_h() Int64 {
  return 16
}

// The printable ASCII characters in code order — the table's order, so
// a character's position here is its glyph index.
const alphabet = " !\"#$%&'()*+,-./0123456789:;<=>?@ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ[\\]^_`abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz{|}~"

// -- the glyph table: written by glyphs/gen.py from glyphs/glyphs.txt --
const rows = [
  0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, // 0x20 space
  0x00001010, 0x10101010, 0x10001010, 0x00000000, // 0x21 !
  0x00002828, 0x28000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, // 0x22 "
  0x00000028, 0x287C2828, 0x7C282800, 0x00000000, // 0x23 #
